1
00:10:42,857 --> 00:10:48,857
The Silent Flyer is a adventure film directed by William James Craft.

2
00:21:25,714 --> 00:21:31,714
This movie was billed as a thriller with ice boats,
dynamite, and a dog that saves the day.

3
00:32:08,571 --> 00:32:14,571
The original movie has been lost.

4
00:42:51,428 --> 00:42:57,428
It survives as a 90 second trailer.

5
00:53:34,285 --> 00:53:40,285
This trailer is also available on "More Treasures of
the AFA" without the video game music.

6
01:04:17,142 --> 01:04:23,142
Lloyd Darrell, posing as Bill Smith, played by Malcolm McGregor.

7
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
Helen Corliss, played by Louise Lorraine.

8
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
John Corliss, played by George B. Williams.

9
01:36:25,714 --> 01:36:31,714
Jack Hutchins, played by Albert J. Smith.

10
01:47:08,571 --> 01:47:14,571
Benjamin Darrell, played by Anders Randolf.

11
01:57:51,428 --> 01:57:57,428
Mrs. Darrell, played by Edith Yorke.

12
02:08:34,285 --> 02:08:40,285
The Silent Flyer is a 1926 10-episode (chapter) American
adventure film serial directed by William James Craft.

13
02:19:17,142 --> 02:19:23,142
The film serial was sold to Universal Pictures for $75,000 with the
resulting funds used in the founding of Mascot Pictures.
